# C4b.3: resume on reconnect, with a change during the outage.
#
# The page joins the live board, moves it once itself, then drops its link.
# While it is away the host moves the board natively (`remote-nudge` asks the
# fixture's `POST /nudge`). The page rejoins as the same subject with the
# retained delegation — the invitation is not spent again — and the change
# it missed comes back as a bell, resumed by diff, without a re-snapshot.
wait
assert snap remote-link == webrtc
assert snap remote-state == open
assert snap remote-revision == 1
act session-remote
settle 1
act invoke-action
settle 1
dom click [data-intent="mere.graphshell/live-fixture/append"]
wait
assert snap action-status ~ Accepted
assert snap remote-revision == 2
assert snap remote-cards == 2
capture c4b3_before_outage
wait
# Down.
act remote-disconnect
wait
assert snap remote-state == disconnected
assert event remote-channel-closed
# The host moves on without us.
act remote-nudge
wait
assert event remote-nudged revision 3
assert snap remote-revision == 2
# Back, as the same subject.
act remote-reconnect
wait
assert snap remote-state == open
assert snap remote-rejoins == 1
assert event remote-rejoined
assert event remote-bell revision 3
assert snap remote-revision == 3
assert snap remote-cards == 3
assert snap remote-resume ~ diff · 2 → 3
capture c4b3_resumed
wait
log c4b3 reconnect receipt complete
